Package: homelab-pgbouncer
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36), pgbouncer
Recommends: homelab-database
Description: PgBouncer connection pooler in front of the shared homelab database
 Configures PgBouncer (scram-sha-256 auth, a static userlist.txt) with a
 `homelab` database entry pointing at a homelab-database-managed Postgres
 backend, local or remote. Config is a single drop-in file activated via
 pgbouncer's own native %include directive -- never hand-edits
 pgbouncer.ini beyond that one line. Ships
 homelab-bootstrap-pgbouncer-entry, a reusable tool other homelab-*
 packages' installers call to register a feature's RUNTIME role's SCRAM
 secret (from homelab-database's homelab-bootstrap-app-role) into
 userlist.txt -- locally, over SSH to a remote pgbouncer host, or by
 printing the exact line for a human to add by hand -- never a
 stored/network admin credential. The migrate role from the split-role
 design is deliberately never registered here -- it connects directly to
 Postgres, bypassing the pooler, on purpose.
